{%
  layout 'theme' title: "Build with Claude"
  , area: "build-with-claude"
  , description: "Describe the website you want and build it with Claude Code, using the real archival CLI. Publishes to a shareable preview URL when you're happy with it."
  , path: "build-with-claude"
%}

<div class="build-with-claude">
  <h1 class="hero-message mb-8">Build it with Claude.</h1>
  <p class="build-description mb-12">
    Describe the site you want. Claude Code interviews you, builds it with the real archival CLI, and publishes it to a
    link you can share.
  </p>

  <div id="bwc" class="bwc-panel">
    <noscript>
      <p class="bwc-note">This page needs JavaScript to hand your session off to Claude Code.</p>
    </noscript>

    <form id="bwc-form" class="bwc-form">
      <label class="bwc-label" for="bwc-brief">
        What are you building? <span class="bwc-optional">Optional</span>
      </label>
      <textarea
        id="bwc-brief"
        class="bwc-textarea"
        rows="3"
        maxlength="600"
        placeholder="A one-page site for my bakery in Joshua Tree — hours, a few photos, and how to find us."
      ></textarea>

      {% comment %}
        Rendered explicitly by src/build-with-claude.ts so the widget can be
        reset: a token is single-use and this page does not navigate away.
      {% endcomment %}
      <div id="bwc-turnstile" class="bwc-turnstile"></div>

      <button
        id="bwc-submit"
        type="submit"
        class="primary-cta bwc-submit"
        data-umami-event="bwc-start"
      >
        Get my build link
      </button>
      <p id="bwc-error" class="bwc-error" hidden></p>
    </form>

    <div id="bwc-result" class="bwc-result" hidden>
      <p class="bwc-note">
        Your site will be reserved at
        <code id="bwc-name" class="bwc-code"></code> for the next two hours.
      </p>

      <a
        id="bwc-deeplink"
        class="primary-cta bwc-launch"
        href="#"
        data-umami-event="bwc-deeplink"
      >
        Open in Claude Code
      </a>
      <p class="bwc-note">
        Opens Claude Code on this computer with the prompt filled in. Nothing is sent until you read it and press enter.
      </p>

      <details class="bwc-details">
        <summary>Prefer a cloud session, or nothing happened?</summary>
        <p class="bwc-note">
          The button needs Claude Code installed on this machine. Otherwise copy this — it starts a session on
          Anthropic's infrastructure:
        </p>
        <div class="bwc-copy-row">
          <pre id="bwc-command" class="bwc-command"></pre>
          <button
            id="bwc-copy"
            type="button"
            class="bwc-copy"
            data-umami-event="bwc-copy-command"
          >
            Copy
          </button>
        </div>
        <p class="bwc-note">
          A cloud session needs
          <a
            href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cloud-environments"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            >a network environment</a
          >
          that allows <code class="bwc-code">api.archival.dev</code> — the default list does not. Publishing fails
          without it.
        </p>
        <p class="bwc-note">
          No Claude Code?
          <a
            href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/quickstart"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
            >Install it here</a
          >, or <a href="https://editor.archival.dev/new">build a site in the editor</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="bwc-fineprint">
    Previews are public and expire if nobody claims them. Every published preview is reviewed. Claude runs on your own
    Anthropic account —
    <a href="/agent/build-site.md">the instructions it follows</a> are public, and work in any coding agent.
  </p>
</div>
